    <item>
      <title>3.3.1. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIPickerView</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.4.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-2-uipickerview/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.4.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-2-uipickerview/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;331-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uipickerview&#34;&gt;3.3.1. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIPickerView&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#331-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uipickerview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;//localhost:1313/gitbook-assets/Screenshot 2023-05-11 at 12.13.48 PM (1).png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now let&amp;rsquo;s open the second screen (ShowViewController). We are going to set up our PickerView &lt;code&gt;moodPicker&lt;/code&gt; now. Let&amp;rsquo;s define an array of Strings having three moods: &amp;ldquo;Happy,&amp;rdquo; &amp;ldquo;Meh,&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Sad.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// moods for moodPicker...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; moods: [String] = [&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Happy&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Meh&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Sad&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;] &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also, let&amp;rsquo;s declare a variable that keeps the selected mode:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; selectedMood = &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Happy&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now it&amp;rsquo;s time to set up the PickerView. To activate a PickerView, the class ShowViewController needs to adopt two &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/sakibnm/iOS/blob/main/10.-protocols&#34;&gt;Protocols&lt;/a&gt;: UIPickerViewDelegate, and UIPickerViewDataSource. UIPickerViewDelegate is the protocol to enable user interactions with the PickerView, and UIPickerViewDataSource is the protocol to access data to display on PickerView.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>3.3.2. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: delegating to ViewController</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.5.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-3-delegating-to-viewcontroller/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.5.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-3-delegating-to-viewcontroller/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;332-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-delegating-to-viewcontroller&#34;&gt;3.3.2. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: delegating to ViewController&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#332-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-delegating-to-viewcontroller&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s enable the action for &lt;code&gt;buttonSendMood&lt;/code&gt; in ShowViewController.swift file. So let&amp;rsquo;s update &lt;code&gt;viewDidLoad()&lt;/code&gt; function and add a new selector method &lt;code&gt;onSendButtonTapped()&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;{% code lineNumbers=&amp;ldquo;true&amp;rdquo; %}&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-swift&#34; data-lang=&#34;swift&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// setting up buttonSendMood...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;override&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;viewDidLoad&lt;/span&gt;() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;super&lt;/span&gt;.viewDidLoad()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//setting the view background to white...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        view.backgroundColor = .white&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt; initializing the UI elements...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        setupLabelMessage()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        setupLabelMoodInstructions()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        setupMoodPicker()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        setupButtonSendMood()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt; setting up constraints...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        initConstraints()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt; add a delegate to on &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;//button send mode tapped...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        buttonSendMood.addTarget(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;, action: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;#selector&lt;/span&gt;(onSendMoodButtonTapped), &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;: .touchUpInside)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;MARK:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt; on send button tapped...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;@objc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;onSendMoodButtonTapped&lt;/span&gt;(){&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;{% endcode %}&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>3.3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIImageView</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.6.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-4-uiimageview/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/3.-our-first-multi-screen-app/3.3.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-1/3.6.-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-part-4-uiimageview/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;333-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uiimageview&#34;&gt;3.3.3. Send data back from Screen 2 to Screen 1: UIImageView&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#333-send-data-back-from-screen-2-to-screen-1-uiimageview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;importing-images-into-the-project&#34;&gt;Importing images into the project&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#importing-images-into-the-project&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Now, let&amp;rsquo;s start working with ImageViews. We need three images for moods: happy, meh, and sad. We will be using the following images in three different sizes: 1x, 2x, and 3x.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;//localhost:1313/gitbook-assets/happy%20%281%29.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; /&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;//localhost:1313/gitbook-assets/meh%20%281%29.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; /&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;//localhost:1313/gitbook-assets/sad%20%281%29.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Download the images from here:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;{% file src=&amp;quot;/gitbook-assets/images (1).zip&amp;quot; %}&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you extract the files, you will see something like the following:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
